Krita Nova 54 - the pop-up palette's color selector matches the docker's

The pop-up palette drew the sRGB triangle by default, whatever the Advanced
Color Selector looked like. Krita can draw it from the Advanced Color
Selector's settings instead (KisVisualColorSelector, "Wide Gamut Selector" in
Configure Krita > Pop-up Palette > Color Selector):

- that is the default now, and existing settings are switched to it once
  (kritarc popuppalette/novaSelectorFollowsACS); it can still be set back;
- the option is called "Same as the Advanced Color Selector";
- Restore Defaults picks it too.

The selector follows changes of the Color Selector Settings (shape, ring or
slider, HSV/HSL/...) as before; in the round palette a slider is drawn as a
ring.
